ion is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Each drift-report entry has a ticket linked `discovered_from` the' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (privilege_posture is missing or a placeholder value; instrument is missing or a placeholder value; justification is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"indeterminate","decision_margin":0.275,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Subject: 'the runner executes the criterion's real Pass-1 finder via `eval_solver.run_case(prompt_id, case, runner=live, repo_root=repo_root)`'","Subject: '`_fired(verdict)` (a finding present) is the observed verdict; a case matching its `expect` in ≥2 of 3 runs REPRODUCES'","Prereq: '`input` is a deterministic, model-free provenance descriptor rendered from the row's stable fields ... It is NOT authored prose and NOT resolved from any store'"],"finding":"The emitter prerequisite writes each spec into a working directory and explicitly excludes writing into `.rebar/evals/`, and derives `input` as a deterministic model-free provenance descriptor (not the plan prompt). The subject plan's admission runner carries the candidate's strict-only fields UNCHANGED, listing them as `prompt`, `model`, `epochs`, `gate`, `coverage_threshold`, `scorers`, and rebuilds `dataset`/`gold_set` from reproducing cases. However, the subject's provenance scheme conflicts: the subject states the emitter embeds `norm_id` for must-fire and `review_event_uuid` for must-not-fire in the case input, which matches the prerequisite's derivation. But the subject also asserts the emitter writes 'one strict-valid candidate spec per criterion, each a `dataset`', whereas the prerequisite emits at most 8 cases spanning both directions in a single dataset — consistent. The genuine inconsistency: the subject's runner executes the criterion's real Pass-1 finder via `eval_solver.run_case(prompt_id, case, ...)`, which requires the case `input` to be a real plan prompt the finder can run against. The prerequisite explicitly states `input` is 'NOT authored prose and NOT resolved from any store' — a synthetic provenance descriptor, not a runnable plan. A finder cannot reproduce a fire/no-fire verdict against a provenance descriptor that contains no plan content.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb8c6a5df4eb91f3f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"SUBJECT: Approach/Run; PREREQ: Approach 'Case payloads are DERIVED'","norm_id":"n069b7a17535d0ed7","priority":0.875,"reason":"prerequisite-coverage-indeterminate","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes",